I'll adversarially verify `bin/similar-causes.py` against its stated contract: reproduce defects with exact commands, and only report what I can demonstrate.Suite is green. Next I'll probe corner cases the acceptance tests likely miss: empty-token queries, output injection, corpus edge cases.Probing argparse quirks (`---`, empty `--corpus`) and whether corpus text can reintroduce verdict language.Rechecking dash-prefixed queries carefully — the piped run may have masked real exit codes.VERDICT: DEFECTIVE

Acceptance suite reconfirmed green: **27/27** (`bash bin/tests/test_similar_causes.sh`). Extra suite also green. Defects below are outside that suite.

