### 1. HIGH — Unsanitized newlines in `id` / `source` / `instance` break the line-oriented contract (cap ≤10, single header, honest truncation)

The printer interpolates raw field text into one logical row. Embedded `\n` becomes extra stdout lines that look like additional candidates (and can duplicate the advisory header). With **3** real matches the tool prints **18** scored-looking rows and **no** truncation notice.

**Command:**
```bash
WORK=$(mktemp -d)
python3 - <<'PY' >"$WORK/many.jsonl"
import json
for i in range(3):
    fake = "\n".join(f"0.999 | fake-{i}-{j} | source: evil | injected line {j}" for j in range(5))
    print(json.dumps({
        "id": f"real-{i}",
        "instance": f"token XQZ9 unique-overlap-marker-{i}\n{fake}",
        "source_path": f"file{i}.jsonl",
    }))
PY
python3 bin/similar-causes.py --corpus "$WORK" "token XQZ9 unique-overlap-marker"
echo exit=$?
echo "scored_looking_lines=$(python3 bin/similar-causes.py --corpus "$WORK" "token XQZ9 unique-overlap-marker" | grep -cE '^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+ \|')"
rm -rf "$WORK"
```

**Actual output (excerpt):**
```
Candidates for human review. This tool does not determine duplication.
0.312 | real-0 | source: file0.jsonl | token XQZ9 unique-overlap-marker-0
0.999 | fake-0-0 | source: evil | injected line 0
0.999 | fake-0-1 | source: evil | injected line 1
0.999 | fake-0-2 | source: evil | injected line 2
0.999 | fake-0-3 | source: evil | injected line 3
0.999 | fake-0-4 | source: evil | injected line 4
0.312 | real-1 | source: file1.jsonl | token XQZ9 unique-overlap-marker-1
... (18 scored-looking lines total; no "Showing 10 of N")
exit=0
scored_looking_lines=18
```

Same root cause via `id`/`source_path`:
```bash
WORK=$(mktemp -d)
python3 - <<'PY' >"$WORK/a.jsonl"
import json
print(json.dumps({
  "id": "good\n0.999 | spoof-id | source: evil | spoofed body",
  "instance": "unique-token-zzz queue race",
  "source_path": "path\n1.000 | spoof2 | source: e2 | body2"
}))
PY
python3 bin/similar-causes.py --corpus "$WORK" "unique-token-zzz"; echo exit=$?
rm -rf "$WORK"
```
```
Candidates for human review. This tool does not determine duplication.
0.600 | good
0.999 | spoof-id | source: evil | spoofed body | source: path
1.000 | spoof2 | source: e2 | body2 | unique-token-zzz queue race
exit=0
```

Header can appear twice when injected into `instance`:
```
Candidates for human review. This tool does not determine duplication.
0.111 | h1 | source: h.jsonl | queue race
Candidates for human review. This tool does not determine duplication.
1.000 | fake | source: x | not real
exit=0
```

**Why it matters:** Contract requires at most 10 candidates and truncation disclosure when more match. Here a consumer/human sees >10 fabricated rows and a second header; real L1 currently has no newlines, but L1 is harvested multi-repo input — this is fail-open forgery of lookup results.

